  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>GitKraft</name>
  <summary>Git client and forge dashboard</summary>
  <description>
    <p>GitKraft is a native Git client written in Rust. Browse history, stage and commit changes, manage branches, stashes and remotes, and inspect diffs.</p>
    <p>It also talks to GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Forgejo and Codeberg, so most of what you would open a web dashboard for is in one window:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Pull requests and issues across your repositories, with review, merge and labels</li>
      <li>Notifications in one inbox, with desktop alerts</li>
      <li>CI runs, jobs and logs with search, plus re-run and cancel</li>
      <li>Activity and contribution graphs</li>
      <li>More than 100 colour themes, light and dark</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Optional AI helpers only write drafts for you to review, and only when you switch them on. Access tokens stay in your system keyring or environment, never in a config file.</p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.sorinirimies.GitKraft.desktop</launchable>
